* NodeForge's generic models: typical values for common classes of part, written for NodeForge
* (not manufacturers' models). Free to use and share. For a real part, import its maker's model.
* Each is named GEN_ and the part it's typical of (the app shows the part's name, under Generic).
* Self-heating (used only when it's on): the power MOSFETs carry their package's junction-case
* resistance RTHJC, case-ambient in free air RTHCA (RthJA - RthJC; a heatsink lowers it) and CTHJ for a
* junction time constant of 10 ms (TO-247), 5 ms (TO-220) or 1 ms (TO-92, SOT-23), with mobility
* (MU), threshold (TCVTH, -5 mV/K) and drift resistance (TRD1) temperature terms, so RDS(on) rises
* about 1.7× from 25 to 150 °C; the rectifiers carry RTH0 = RthJA (lead-mounted) and CTH0 for 0.1 s.
*
* Small-signal switching diode (1N4148 class): 100 V, fast (a few ns)
.model GEN_1N4148 D(IS=4n N=1.9 RS=0.6 BV=100 IBV=5u CJO=2p VJ=0.7 M=0.33 TT=6n)
* General-purpose rectifier (1N4007 class): 1 A, 1000 V, slow recovery (µs)
.model GEN_1N4007 D(IS=7n N=1.8 RS=0.04 BV=1000 IBV=5u CJO=15p VJ=0.7 M=0.4 TT=3u RTH0=50 CTH0=0.002)
* Ultrafast rectifier (UF4007 class): 1 A, 1000 V, 50 ns recovery
.model GEN_UF4007 D(IS=1n N=1.9 RS=0.06 BV=1000 IBV=5u CJO=15p VJ=0.7 M=0.4 TT=50n RTH0=50 CTH0=0.002)
* Schottky rectifier (1N5819 class): 1 A, 40 V, low drop, no stored charge
.model GEN_1N5819 D(IS=30u N=1.05 RS=0.15 BV=40 IBV=1m CJO=110p VJ=0.35 M=0.4 TT=0 RTH0=50 CTH0=0.002)
